2026-11-06T03:02:10.3746672Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3755650Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3756491Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3757227Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3757534Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3757739Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3758082Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3758565Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3759522Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3759869Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3760059Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3760491Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3760752Z 
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3760984Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:02:10.3761341Z   $ sh ./install-nix
